#ASSERT `s 171ZC(1) the notice condition for payments of statutory paternity pay is met` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZC(1) the notice condition for payments of statutory paternity pay is met` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZC(2) the notice shall be in writing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZC(2) the notice shall be in writing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZD -- liability`

#ASSERT `s 171ZD(1) the liability to make payments of statutory paternity pay is the person's` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZD(1) the liability to make payments of statutory paternity pay is the person's` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZE(1), (2), (3) -- rate, choice of weeks, qualifying period`

#ASSERT `s 171ZE(1) the weekly rate of statutory paternity pay in pounds` (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(1) the weekly rate of statutory paternity pay in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the choice; the weeks chosen are within the qualifying period; regulations permit one week or two separate weeks.
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE two consecutive weeks` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE two consecutive weeks` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE one week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE one week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE one week` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE two non-consecutive periods of a week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(2) the person may choose the weeks in respect of which statutory paternity pay is payable` `s 171ZE two non-consecutive periods of a week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the case; the date of the child's birth (or the first of several); the date of the placement (or the first of several).
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the day on which the qualifying period begins` `s 171ZE a birth` (Date 10 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 10 11 2026
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the day on which the qualifying period begins` `s 171ZE a placement for adoption` (Date 10 11 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the least length of the qualifying period in days` EQUALS 56
-- Arguments: the length of the qualifying period determined by regulations, in days.
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the qualifying period determined by regulations is long enough` 56 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the qualifying period determined by regulations is long enough` 57 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3) the qualifying period determined by regulations is long enough` 55 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZE(3A) to (7) -- weeks in which pay is not payable`

-- Arguments: pay or leave in part of that week; pay or leave in respect of the child before that week.
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3A) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3A) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3A) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZE(3A) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: purpose to care for the child at the beginning of the week; purpose to support the other person.
